{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## AC1 pre-flight census + AC4 AST scan — recorded evidence\n\nRun in `.rebar/worktrees/impl-ed5a`, base `e096a33d3b7` (0 ahead / 0 behind `origin/main`),\nvenv metadata `nava_rebar-0.14.0.dist-info`, `rebar.__version__ == 0.14.0`.\n\n### AC1 — pre-flight census, BEFORE the first edit\n\n```\ngit grep -n -E '_engine_support\\.resolver|_engine_support import resolver' -- src tests scripts\n```\n\n**19 lines across 15 files** — exactly the population the plan declares, so the plan was NOT\nstale and editing proceeded. Breakdown by the plan's five shapes, all counts matching:\n\n| Shape | Description | Plan | Measured |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| A | module-level `from … import resolve_ticket_id` | 2 | 2 |\n| B | function-local, same import | 9 | 9 |\n| C | function-local `resolve_ticket_dir_name` | 3 | 3 |\n| D | multi-line parenthesised | 1 | 1 |\n| E | fully-qualified attribute call | 4 | 4 |\n| | **total** | **19** | **19** |\n\nZero sites in `src/` and zero in `scripts/` — the whole population is under `tests/`.\n\n### Shape-E binding risk — measured, not assumed\n\nAll 4 shape-E files import only bare `import rebar` and reach the submodule as an incidentally\nbound attribute. Re-measured in this worktree before relying on it:\n\n```\nrebar._ids bound: True\nresolve_ticket_id: True\n```\n\nso rewriting `rebar._engine_support.resolver.resolve_ticket_id(…)` to\n`rebar._ids.resolve_ticket_id(…)` is safe in those 4 files without adding an import.\n\n### AC4 — AST scan over every `._processors` importer\n\nScan over every file matching `from (rebar\\.reducer)?\\._processors import`, checking for imports\nof `process_status`, `process_signature`, `process_key_event`, `_rederive_keyring_keys`,\n`_fold_claimed_session`, `_fold_close_metadata`, `_fold_plan_review_phase`:\n\n```\nscanned 13 importer file(s)\nVIOLATIONS: none\n```\n\nConfirms the plan's finding that the `reducer._processors` half of this story was already\ncompleted by `374cc2f22b1`; AC4 stands as a regression guard, not as work performed here.\n\n### AC5 — regression guard\n\n`tests/unit/test_processors_status_split.py` absent, and\n`pytest --collect-only -q tests/unit/test_plan_review_phase_reducer.py -k status_fold_replay_equivalence`\ncollects exactly one node (`test_status_fold_replay_equivalence`; 1/10 collected, 9 deselected).\n\n### Post-edit ACs already green\n\n- **AC2** — the census grep over `src tests scripts` exits **1** printing nothing.\n- **AC3** — `import rebar._engine_support.resolver` raises\n  `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'rebar._engine_support.resolver'`.\n- **AC6** — `docs/bash-migration.md` contains 0 occurrences; `git status --porcelain docs/archive/`\n  is empty, so the historical record is untouched as the plan requires.\n\nAC7 (`make verify` exits 0) is pending the serial verify slot.\n"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793413071311423413,"uuid":"7809a042-9eed-458e-932f-48541e893b34"}